prompt:
Edit this image. It is a crop of a finished hand-painted top-down JRPG map (rich hi-bit pixel-art painting, classic steep 3/4 top-down view). Scale: 48 image pixels = one map tile; a standing person would be about 1.5 tiles (72 px) tall. Some small objects were pasted on top of the painting as separate flat sprites, and they look stuck on: flat lighting, a different pixel style, the wrong size and no shadow. The pasted objects are: 4 sacks, 2 small stones, 8 crates, 5 barrels, 2 bookshelfs, 1 net.
Repaint ONLY those objects so they become part of the painting. Every one of them must still be there and clearly visible after the edit (do not remove any, not even the small ones):
- the same place: each object stays exactly where its sprite is, standing on the same spot, its base where the sprite's base is, inside its own tile;
- a natural size for the tile scale: sack: 0.6 wide, 0.5 tall; small stone: a small stone about 0.35 wide; crate: 0.7 wide, 0.7 tall; barrel: 0.6 wide, 0.8 tall; bookshelf: a wooden shelf 0.9 wide, 1.2 tall; net: a heap of fishing net about 0.9 wide lying on the ground;
- the same soft light from the upper left as the rest of the painting, the same palette, textures and brushwork, crisp pixel clusters like the surroundings;
- a soft contact shadow on the ground right under and slightly to the lower right of each object.
Keep EVERYTHING else exactly as it is, pixel for pixel: ground, paths, buildings, walls, cliffs, water, plants and their edges must not move, change colour or be redrawn. Do not add any other objects, people, animals, lamps or light effects. No text. Even albedo lighting as in the input: no night, no glow, no light pools, no vignette.
